WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.507
Lists are great when position matters.

00:00:02.507 --> 00:00:09.667
Dictionaries are better when labels matter, and sets are useful when uniqueness matters.

00:00:09.667 --> 00:00:18.037
With a list, scores zero means “the first value.” With a dictionary, student score lets the key itself describe the

00:00:18.037 --> 00:00:23.471
meaning. A set is different again: it focuses on distinct values rather than position.

00:00:23.984 --> 00:00:31.296
In analytics, dictionaries often represent records or counts, while sets help with unique categories, IDs,

00:00:31.296 --> 00:00:33.685
and group comparisons.
